  "frozen": {
    "date": "2026-10-14",
    "key": "mw-write-face-guard",
    "source": ".agenticdoc/mw-write-face-guard/evidence/research/design-glob-intersection-20261014.md §5",
    "normative_decisions": "design.md D-001/D-006/D-111/D-112 + RQ-D1 §3.1/§3.2/§3.3/§4.4",
    "extended": "2026-10-14: §3.2 fallback list + mixed-entry order + syntax-blind comma split (P17–P23 / V49–V57), per design.md D-111/D-112 and evidence/PM-parity-differential-20261014.md; V58 (state-machine fallback pair + provable conflict), per evidence/PM-parity-differential-20261014.md section 7",
    "owner": "PM (single writer). Any semantic change to this file is a contract change and must go back to the PM."
  },
  "counts": {
    "parse": 23,
    "overlap": 59,
    "overlap_note": "RQ-D1 §5 的 48 条向量 = 表中 47 条 + V04 拆成 ci/cs 两行（V04 的期望值本身依 caseInsensitive 而变）；逐 kind：overlap 34 / none 13 / reject 8 / serial_only 1 / unsupported 3（后两类扩写见 D-111）"
  },
  "protocol": {
    "entries_placeholder": {
      "$REPO": "absolute path of the repository root at test time",
      "$OUTSIDE": "an absolute path guaranteed NOT to be under $REPO (e.g. a temp dir outside the repo)"
    },
    "parse_kinds": {
      "entries": "ok; expect.entries is the normalized allow list, order preserved, duplicates preserved",
      "unknown": "no `write_face:` head line at all -> undeclared (D-003 serial-only; the overlap operator is NOT called)",
      "reject": "fail-closed; expect.code is the stable refusal code"
    },
    "expect_kinds": {
      "overlap": "the two faces share at least one lexically-provable path; expect.sample_globfree states whether the returned witness must contain no glob magic",
      "none": "lexically provable empty intersection",
      "reject": "one side fails parsing; expect.side says which ('a'|'b'); expect.code is the refusal code",
      "serial_only": "the row carries no write_face declaration; the operator must not be asked to return None for it (D-003)",
      "unsupported": "at least one side carries unsupported syntax (§3.2) and no conflict is provable; callers MUST treat it as overlap (D-006/D-111)"
    },
    "magic_chars": ["*", "?", "[", "]", "{", "}"]
  },
  "notes": [
    "Only the *kind* of each overlap outcome is asserted, not the exact witness string: several valid witnesses exist and pinning one would freeze an implementation detail rather than the contract.",
    "Instead, every `overlap` case asserts the returned witness is glob-free (sample_globfree), so a placeholder such as '<unknown>' or a pattern echo is not accepted as a witness.",
    "`write_face: -` (dash-only value, optional surrounding spaces) means undeclared, exactly like a missing head line: it is the authoring convention for 'not specified' used by the existing task books (`- 依赖: -`). An empty value (`write_face:`) with no dash is a misconfiguration and is refused.",
    "deny never participates in the overlap decision (RQ-D1 §3.2): V37/V38 assert that a deny covering the whole intersection still reports overlap.",
    "D-111 (2026-10-14, PM parity differential): parse-time hard rule violations (`write-face-escape` / `write-face-invalid-entry` / `write-face-outside-base`) take precedence over an unsupported-syntax entry AND the verdict must not depend on entry order (V52–V56). At intersection time a provable conflict wins over unsupported syntax (V57); `Unsupported` means 'cannot decide', not 'decided overlap without a witness'.",
    "D-112 (2026-10-14): the entry list is `split(',')` on the raw head value, then each field is trimmed and parsed on its own. Splitting is syntax-blind - brackets/braces/quotes never protect a comma, and an unterminated `[` never swallows later fields (P22/P23). P16 keeps its code under this rule because `\"a` is the first field and is refused as `write-face-invalid-entry`.",
    "V58 (2026-10-14) pins the section 3.2 state-machine fallback at intersection time: a pair whose product exceeds the state limit must be deferred per pair, not abort the whole search, so a later provably-conflicting pair still yields an overlap (D-111; PM-parity-differential section 7). Its 601 character entry ('x/' repeated 300 times, then 'x') is written inline on purpose: the corpus expands only $REPO/$OUTSIDE, and one more macro would be one more expansion rule to get wrong. The deferred *reason string* is deliberately NOT pinned, so vectors that differ only in that string (unsupported-syntax vs glob-product-state-limit) are not corpus rows."
  ],
  "parse": [
    { "name": "P01 single entry", "head": ["write_face: packages/x/**"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["packages/x/**"] } },
    { "name": "P02 missing head", "head": ["# T-01", "", "- type: coding"], "expect": { "kind": "unknown" } },
    { "name": "P03 dash only", "head": ["write_face: -"], "expect": { "kind": "unknown" }, "note": "authoring 'not specified' marker" },
    { "name": "P04 present but empty", "head": ["write_face:"], "expect": { "kind": "reject", "code": "write-face-empty" } },
    { "name": "P05 two entries", "head": ["write_face: a/**, b/c.ts"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["a/**", "b/c.ts"] } },
    { "name": "P06 empty entries ignored", "head": ["write_face: a/**,,"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["a/**"] } },
    { "name": "P07 strip leading ./", "head": ["write_face: ./packages/x/**"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["packages/x/**"] } },
    { "name": "P08 collapse empty segment", "head": ["write_face: packages//x/**"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["packages/x/**"] } },
    { "name": "P09 backslash is a separator", "head": ["write_face: src\\x\\**"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["src/x/**"] } },
    { "name": "P10 strip trailing slash", "head": ["write_face: packages/x/"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["packages/x"] } },
    { "name": "P11 collapse repeated **", "head": ["write_face: a/**/**"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["a/**"] } },
    { "name": "P12 absolutize inside base", "head": ["write_face: $REPO/packages/x/**"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["packages/x/**"] } },
    { "name": "P13 negated entry refused", "head": ["write_face: !a/**"], "expect": { "kind": "reject", "code": "write-face-invalid-entry" } },
    { "name": "P14 parent escape refused", "head": ["write_face: a/../b/**"], "expect": { "kind": "reject", "code": "write-face-escape" } },
    { "name": "P15 absolute outside base refused", "head": ["write_face: $OUTSIDE/packages/x/**"], "expect": { "kind": "reject", "code": "write-face-outside-base" } },
    { "name": "P16 quoted comma refused", "head": ["write_face: \"a,b\""], "expect": { "kind": "reject", "code": "write-face-invalid-entry" } },
    { "name": "P17 illegal class is not a parse error", "head": ["write_face: src/[a-"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["src/[a-"] }, "note": "D-111: unsupported syntax is an intersection-time fallback, not a parse rule" },
    { "name": "P18 extglob negation is not a parse error", "head": ["write_face: src/!(x)"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["src/!(x)"] } },
    { "name": "P19 extglob plus() is not a parse error", "head": ["write_face: src/+(x)"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["src/+(x)"] } },
    { "name": "P20 extglob at() is not a parse error", "head": ["write_face: src/@(x)"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["src/@(x)"] } },
    { "name": "P21 unclosed brace is not a parse error", "head": ["write_face: src/{a,b"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["src/{a", "b"] }, "note": "D-112: the entry list is split on commas BEFORE any pattern parsing (syntax-blind). The comma inside an unclosed brace still splits, so the second field is the fragment `b`; that is intentional - a fragment can only ADD allow entries, so its error direction is fail-closed" },
    { "name": "P22 unsupported entry keeps position next to a valid one", "head": ["write_face: src/[a-, src/ok.ts"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["src/[a-", "src/ok.ts"] }, "note": "D-112: an unterminated `[` must NOT swallow the following field" },
    { "name": "P23 comma is never pattern content", "head": ["write_face: src/[a-, src/b].ts, src/ok.ts"], "expect": { "kind": "entries", "entries": ["src/[a-", "src/b].ts", "src/ok.ts"] }, "note": "D-112 regression: a syntax-aware splitter would let `[` swallow `a-, src/b]` as a character class and merge three declared entries into one" }
  ],
